{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/371603-looking-for-help-to-build-a-town-setting","id":371603,"title":"Looking for help to build a Town Setting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-15T17:47:19-08:00","id":371603,"title":"Looking for help to build a Town Setting","content":"I fell inlove with the Ray Bradbury narrative and his idea of little towns with big stories. I decided to make something in a very similar way, very in the way of Something Wicked This Way Comes or little suburbia. any advices as for reference books to build a town or programs to make a map of the town?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T22:49:00-08:00","id":371926,"title":"","content":"I ran a town based game for a year that's just about to end so I'd be more than happy to give you some tips. Its a good idea to have some history reference for how/why the town was built so you can get an idea of what supernatural powers might have influenced. But the biggest thing I feel is the importance of locations. I find it even more so then the typical city set chronicle to have pre-established locations as while in a city campaign you can pull out the name of some random place you make up and place it in your chronicle, but in a town which is much smaller you defiantly want to research what are the well known land marks, buildings and so on.<br /> <br /> From there you should come up with what supernatural elements have ties to what areas, what may be some things about it that humans might not know exist. For example the game I ran was set in my hometown and in said town is a large pizza restaurant that's been here for years. For awhile not many cars could be seen in the parking lot yet the place was and has still been opened. My mom liked to joke that it was/became a front for the mob, so I got the idea to make it the haven for a group of Giovanni that had moved in and were attempting to take control of the town from the local kindred population.<br /> <br /> You might also want to tone down the amount of power players you have depending on what type of game. For vampire maybe only 5 or 6 vampires live in the town, Werewolf you could have a campaign were most of combat takes place in the umbra and so on. A good concept to go for is &quot;something big happens in a place that isn't very important because not many eyes will see it and be able to move to stop it&quot;. <br /> <br /> And my last bit of advice is have very well fleshed out NPCs as the players will more than likely be interacting with the same ones on multiple occasions and you don't want your players to not care about them.<br /> <br /> Hope that helps and good luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2256-goblin404","name":"Goblin404","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2256_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T01:15:05-08:00","id":372098,"title":"","content":"While they are nWoD and slightly off-topic, check out <i>Block by Bloody Block</i> and <i>Damnation City. </i>They're both guides to building settings, designed around districts and landmarks; while slightly larger in scale than what you're looking for, they're valuable resources nonetheless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T10:45:55-08:00","id":372730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goblin404</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/371603-looking-for-help-to-build-a-town-setting?p=371926#post371926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might also want to tone down the amount of power players you have depending on what type of game. For vampire maybe only 5 or 6 vampires live in the town, Werewolf you could have a campaign were most of combat takes place in the umbra and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good idea. Rather than having an inexplicably high population supernatural beasties in a given area, I would come up with a handful and really flesh them out into regular characters. Heck, I would do that with mundane people as well. In a small town everyone knows each other. Figure out how the different characters in your game know each other. Have they learned to play nice or are contentions reaching a breaking point? Rumors and secrets are also important. Since everyone knows each other, unpleasant truths tend to circulate, often due to boredom rather than malice.<br /> <br /> Real-world geography can help here too. Learn about the history of the area your town is set in. This often gives me good ideas for adding texture. If lumber was big back in the 40's and 50's, factor that in by incorporating an old mill as a haven or how the local werewolves narrowly lost a fight with a Pentex-backed logging corporation. Maybe some obscure celebrity from the town and her endorsements are splashed everywhere, or each year there is a UFO convention because some strange space rock was found out in the woods back in the 80s. I am curious to see where this goes...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T14:53:51-08:00","id":391884,"title":"","content":"Another resource to look at is the Dresden Files RPG by Evil Hat Gaming Studio - it models the Harry Dresden Novels written by Jim Butcher. There is a whole chapter or two in the core or in the other book for it on building a city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}